ReadyToRun images for witos (plan step R9): crossgen2 names a native image's operating system in its machine field
(IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_NATIVE_OS_OVERRIDE), and TargetOS.WitOS had no mark, so --targetos witos stopped with
NotImplementedException. WitOS's CoreCLR is built for the musl triple, which defines __linux__, and pedecoder.h takes
Linux's mark from it: the guest accepts Linux's images (S8.2), so crossgen2 writes that mark for witos too.

--- a/src/coreclr/tools/aot/ILCompiler.ReadyToRun/ObjectWriter/TargetExtensions.cs
+++ b/src/coreclr/tools/aot/ILCompiler.ReadyToRun/ObjectWriter/TargetExtensions.cs
@@ -111,6 +111,10 @@
                 case TargetOS.Linux:
                     return MachineOSOverride.Linux;
 
+                // WitOS's CoreCLR takes Linux's mark: its triple is musl's, which defines __linux__ (pedecoder.h).
+                case TargetOS.WitOS:
+                    return MachineOSOverride.Linux;
+
                 case TargetOS.OSX:
                 case TargetOS.MacCatalyst:
